(Same 3 occurrences at `v1.2.3`.) So the bundle is `Ghostty.app` but the Mach-O is `Ghostty.app/Contents/MacOS/ghostty`, and `GHOSTTY_BIN_DIR` = `…/Ghostty.app/Contents/MacOS`. Shell integration then appends it to `PATH` (`src/shell-integration/{bash,zsh,fish,elvish,nushell}/…`), and elvish/nushell explicitly build `$GHOSTTY_BIN_DIR/ghostty`.

---

## 3. `+action` implementation, `+ssh-cache`, `+ssh`

Registry: `src/cli/ghostty.zig` — an `Action` enum whose `runMain` switch dispatches to per-action `run(alloc)`. Detection: `src/cli/action.zig` `detectIter` — an arg is an action iff `arg[0] == '+'`; more than one is `DetectError.MultipleActions`, unknown is `InvalidAction`. Special cases: `--version` → `.version`, `--help`/`-h` → fallback `.help`, `-e` → `abort_if_no_action`.

`src/cli/` on main (28 files): `version, help, list-fonts, list-keybinds, list-themes, list-colors, list-actions, ssh, ssh-cache, edit-config, show-config, explain-config, validate-config, show-face, crash-report, boo, new-window, toggle-quick-terminal` (+ support files `action.zig`, `args.zig`, `diagnostics.zig`, `Pager.zig`, `CommaSplitter.zig`, `tui.zig`), plus a `ssh-cache/` subdir containing `DiskCache.zig` and `Entry.zig`.

**`+ssh-cache`** (`src/cli/ssh_cache.zig`) — inspects/maintains the terminfo cache. Doc comment:

> Manage the SSH terminfo cache for automatic remote host setup. … The cache stores destinations (a hostname or user@hostname) along with timestamps.

Options: `--clear`, `--add=<dest>`, `--remove=<dest>`, `--prune=<duration>` (`s/m/h/d/w/y`), plus a positional destination query; bare `ghostty +ssh-cache` lists everything; a query matching nothing exits 1. `--host=X` is accepted but deprecated in favour of the positional.

**Cache file path** — `src/cli/ssh-cache/DiskCache.zig`:

```zig
/// Returns the default path for the cache for a given program.
///
/// On all platforms, this is `${XDG_STATE_HOME}/ghostty/ssh_cache`.
pub fn defaultPath(alloc: Allocator, program: []const u8) ![]const u8 {
    ...
    const state_dir: []const u8 = xdg.state(global.io(), alloc, &environ_map, .{ .subdir = program });
    ...
    return try std.fs.path.join(alloc, &.{ state_dir, "ssh_cache" });
}
```

Both call sites pass `"ghostty"` (`ssh_cache.zig:137`, `ssh.zig:247`). `xdg.state` (`src/os/xdg.zig:40`) uses env `XDG_STATE_HOME`, Windows fallback `LOCALAPPDATA`, `default_subdir = ".local/state"`. **So on macOS with no `XDG_STATE_HOME` set: `~/.local/state/ghostty/ssh_cache`.** Format is line-based `hostname|timestamp|terminfo_version`, chmod `0600`, exclusive-locked, written atomically, capped at 512KB. The wording "on all platforms" is verbatim and identical at `v1.2.3` — there is no Application Support variant.

**`+ssh`** (`src/cli/ssh.zig`, added `484d6ec6`, Jon Parise, 2026-05-04) — a drop-in `ssh` wrapper. Usage banner:

```
Usage: ghostty +ssh [flags] [--] <ssh args...>

Flags:
  --forward-env[=bool]  Enable TERM / SendEnv forwarding. Default: true.
  --terminfo[=bool]     Install Ghostty terminfo on first connect. Default: true.
  --cache[=bool]        Use the terminfo install cache. Default: true.
  --ssh=<path>          Path to the ssh binary. Default: first `ssh` on PATH.
  --verbose             Print +ssh status lines to stderr.
  --help                Show full help.
```

Per the commit message, before exec'ing ssh it forwards `TERM=xterm-256color` + `SendEnv` of `COLORTERM`/`TERM_PROGRAM`/`TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION`, and installs `xterm-ghostty` terminfo on the remote, consulting the same `ssh-cache` so it doesn't re-upload. Unrecognised args are forwarded verbatim to the real `ssh` (`parseManuallyHook` stops flag parsing at `--` or the first non-`--` arg). `+ssh` runs automatically from shell integration when `shell-integration-features` includes `ssh-terminfo`.

---

## 4. `ghostty_init` does **not** dispatch actions — this corrects your key hypothesis

`include/ghostty.h` published API (identical at main and `v1.2.3`, lines 891–892):

```c
int ghostty_init(uintptr_t, char**);
void ghostty_cli_try_action(void);
```

`src/main_c.zig` on main:

```zig
/// Initialize ghostty global state.
pub export fn ghostty_init(argc: usize, argv: [*][*:0]u8) c_int {
    assert(builtin.link_libc);
    global.init(.{ .c = .{ .argc = argc, .argv = argv, .environ = ... } }) catch |err| {
        std.log.err("failed to initialize ghostty error={}", .{err});
        return 1;
    };
    return 0;
}

/// Runs an action if it is specified. If there is no action this returns
/// false. If there is an action then this doesn't return.
pub export fn ghostty_cli_try_action() void {
    const action = global.action() orelse return;
    std.log.info("executing CLI action={}", .{action});
    posix.system.exit(action.run(global.alloc()) catch |err| {
        std.log.err("CLI action failed error={}", .{err});
        posix.system.exit(1);
    });
    posix.system.exit(0);
}
```

At `35e1a016` and `v1.3.1` the same split exists with the older `state`-global shape (`std.os.argv = argv[0..argc]; state.init()` / `state.action orelse return`).

So the division of labour is:
- **`ghostty_init(argc, argv)`** takes argc/argv and, inside `global.init`, *detects and stores* the action — `src/global.zig`: `self.action = switch (opts) { .main, .c => try cli.action.detectArgs(cli.ghostty.Action, self.alloc, self.args), .tool => null }`. Note `.c` (the libghostty path) is explicitly included. It also silences stderr logging when an action is present. It returns non-zero on an invalid/ambiguous action — which is exactly the error message `main.swift` prints.
- **`ghostty_cli_try_action()`** is what runs the action and calls `exit()`.

**Practical answer to your question:** an executable linking libghostty and calling `ghostty_init(argc, argv)` **followed by `ghostty_cli_try_action()`** is a working `ghostty` CLI. `ghostty_init` alone is not sufficient — it would parse the action and then fall through to your own code. Both symbols are exported from libghostty and both are in the public `ghostty.h`, at every ref checked including `v1.2.3`.

---

## 5. libghostty for macOS contains the CLI action code — yes

`src/build/GhosttyLib.zig`, `initStatic`:

```zig
const lib = b.addLibrary(.{
    .name = "ghostty",
    .root_module = b.createModule(.{
        .root_source_file = b.path("src/main_c.zig"),
        ...
```

`initShared` uses the same root; `initMacOSUniversal` lipos two `initStatic` builds. `src/build/GhosttyXCFramework.zig` builds `GhosttyKit.xcframework` from `GhosttyLib.initMacOSUniversal` (universal) or `initStatic` (native), plus iOS/iOS-sim `initStatic`.

The import chain is unconditional: `src/main_c.zig` → `@import("global.zig")` → `src/global.zig` → `const cli = @import("cli.zig")` → `src/cli.zig` → `pub const ghostty = @import("cli/ghostty.zig")` → which imports `ssh.zig`, `ssh_cache.zig`, and every other action module, and whose `Action.runMain` switch is reachable from `ghostty_cli_try_action`. There is **no build-config gate** separating lib from exe here.

So: `+ssh-cache` and `+ssh` are compiled **into libghostty**, not only into the standalone `ghostty` exe target (`src/build/GhosttyExe.zig`). This is precisely why the macOS app binary works as the CLI — there is only one binary and it links the static lib.

---

## 6. Which version first shipped `+ssh`

| ref | `src/cli/ssh.zig` | `ssh` in `Action` enum | `ssh_cache.zig` |
|---|---|---|---|
| `main` | ✅ 200 | ✅ | ✅ |
| `35e1a016` (2026-07-10) | ✅ 200 | ✅ | ✅ |
| `v1.3.1` (`332b2aef`, 2026-03-13) | ❌ 404 | ❌ | ✅ |
| `v1.3.0` | ❌ 404 | ❌ | ✅ |
| `v1.2.3` | ❌ 404 | ❌ | ✅ |

- **`+ssh` is present at `35e1a0160c4f...` and on `main`.**
- **`+ssh` is NOT present at `v1.3.1`.** It was added 2026-05-04 (`484d6ec6`), ~7 weeks *after* the v1.3.1 commit date of 2026-03-13.
- **No tagged release ships `+ssh` yet.** The full tag list is `v1.3.1, v1.3.0, v1.2.3, v1.2.2, v1.2.1, v1.2.0, v1.1.3, v1.1.2, v1.1.1, v1.1.0, v1.0.1, v1.0.0, tip` — `v1.3.1` is the newest semver tag, and it predates the commit. So `+ssh` is main-only / `tip`-only. **Could not verify** a future version number for it; there is no `v1.4.x` tag to point at.
- **`+ssh-cache` is much older** — present at every tag checked back through `v1.2.3`, with the same `${XDG_STATE_HOME}/ghostty/ssh_cache` path and the same `DiskCache.defaultPath(alloc, "ghostty")` contract.

---

## Bottom line for an embedder

Linking libghostty (e.g. GhosttyKit 1.2.3, which workroom already embeds) and calling `ghostty_init(argc, argv)` **then** `ghostty_cli_try_action()` gives you a fully working `ghostty` CLI, including `+ssh-cache`. That has been true since at least `v1.2.3` — both symbols are in the published C API there. `+ssh` specifically requires a `main`-tracking libghostty; it is in no released tag.

